{
  "analysis": "Network connectivity works (got HTTP 200 from YouTube). apt is available. I need to install yt-dlp, ffmpeg, tesseract-ocr, and pip. Let me start by updating apt and installing the core tools.",
  "plan": "Run apt-get update, then install ffmpeg, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-eng, and python3-pip. Installing yt-dlp via pip after. This may take a while, so I'll set a longer duration.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update 2>&1 | tail -5\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "apt-get update succeeded. Now I need to install ffmpeg, tesseract-ocr, and pip to proceed with downloading and OCR.",
  "plan": "Install ffmpeg, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-eng, and python3-pip via apt. This is a larger install so I'll give it more time.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y ffmpeg tesseract-ocr tesseract-ocr-eng python3-pip 2>&1 | tail -15\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The apt install failed because there's not enough free space in /var/cache/apt/archives. I need to check disk space and clean up. The 323MB download plus 1092MB install needs space. Let me check available space and clean apt cache.",
  "plan": "Check disk usage with df -h. Then clean apt cache with apt-get clean. If still insufficient, I may need to install to a different location or use pip to install yt-dlp without huge dependencies. Let me first assess space.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -h / /tmp /var 2>&1; echo '---'; du -sh /var/cache/apt/archives 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The overlay filesystem reports 0 available space (956G used of 984G). This is likely a quota/full disk. I need to find what's consuming space and free some, or find an alternative approach. Let me investigate the disk usage to find large directories.",
  "plan": "Find large files/directories consuming space with du. Check /app, /var, /tmp. Determine if I can free space or if I need a different strategy (e.g., download video to a location, but disk is full everywhere). First investigate.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "du -sh /* 2>/dev/null | sort -rh | head -20\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Strange discrepancy: df reports 956G used / 0 available, but du shows only ~180M actually used. This is a fuse-overlayfs reporting artifact where df reflects the backing store, not the writable overlay. The apt failure says not enough free space for 323MB of archives. I need to determine the real writable capacity. Let me test actual write capability and check the mount.",
  "plan": "Test writing a real file to see how much space is truly available. Check df -i for inodes. Examine mount options. If genuinely constrained, I'll pursue a lighter-weight approach - perhaps installing yt-dlp via pip (small) and using a minimal frame extraction method.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -i / 2>&1; echo '---write test---'; dd if=/dev/zero of=/tmp/testfile bs=1M count=100 2>&1; echo exit=$?; ls -la /tmp/testfile; rm -f /tmp/testfile\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    }
  ]
}

